/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2817:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/7/code.py:129:    Decode the 3x3 contour glyph into a 16x16 rhombic lattice whose two diagonal axes use different periods, then stamp the motif in maroon at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2818:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/7/code.py:138:    - Fill a black 16x16 canvas by sampling that tile in diagonal coordinates, with `u=(row+col) mod 3` and `v=(row-col) mod 2`.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2819:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/7/code.py:142:    - The contour glyph now controls a diagonal coordinate system twice: its 3-row phase ordering sets one family of slanted lattice lines, while its first two phase columns set a different 2-phase alternation on the opposite diagonal family.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2820:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/7/code.py:160:    out = _tile_fill_diagonal_anisotropic(out_shape, phase_colors)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2821:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2d0172a1/17/code.py:587:        mode = \"horizontal\" if compact or random.random() < 0.8 else \"diagonal\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2822:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2d0172a1/17/code.py:589:        mode = \"horizontal\" if compact or random.random() < 0.9 else \"diagonal\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2823:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/45a5af55/12/code.py:29:   - With t=2 this removes a 3-cell right triangle from each corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2824:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/45a5af55/12/code.py:46:  forced to be >= 2 so the diagonal cuts are visually obvious in most samples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2825:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/45a5af55/12/code.py:190:    \"\"\"Mask for a square after removing a 45-degree corner triangle of depth `thick` at each outer corner.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2826:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/45a5af55/12/code.py:259:    # diagonal cut deeper than one pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2827:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/15/code.py:7:#    - The scene still contains one thick anti-diagonal path band, one top-left\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2828:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/15/code.py:298:    \"\"\"Return a thick meandering anti-diagonal band.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2829:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/42/code.py:21:#       1. gap_len = abs(left_arm_len - right_arm_len), measured from the two diagonals meeting\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2830:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/42/code.py:60:#   - The new gap-length helper assumes the spike has exactly two diagonal border arms that can be\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2831:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/42/code.py:153:    \"\"\"Return the absolute difference between the two diagonal arm lengths at the spike.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2832:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/42/code.py:177:    - skip N cells past the spike, where N is the diagonal-arm length difference,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2833:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/1/code.py:12:#    - D1 change: replace the edge head with a fixed 2-pixel diagonal corner marker. The matching\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2834:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_co