path: approach + alongside + diagonal exit tail\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2926:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/19/code.py:26:#       - draw only the visible prefix near the obstacle: the 2 diagonal approach cells plus the 2 straight alongside cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2927:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/19/code.py:32:#     - both approach and alongside are forced to be present, so the new arc is not reducible to a single diagonal or a single straight stub\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2928:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/19/code.py:60:# - the approach+alongside route is at least 3 cells long in raw form and contains both a diagonal run and a straight run\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2929:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/19/code.py:349:    assert first in (\"FL\", \"FR\"), f\"approach must start diagonally, got {first}\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2930:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:28:#   3. The marker's whole bbox is translated by one pixel per step along that diagonal,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2931:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:29:#      creating a staircase-like diagonal strip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2932:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:35:#     (+1,+1), and the plus disappears in the output. One long diagonal strip may already be\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2933:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:39:# - Marker count is constrained to 2-4, matching the four diagonal quadrants. This keeps the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2934:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:41:# - Seed shapes are limited to 1x2 or 2x1. That is deliberate: with one-pixel diagonal shifts,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2935:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:48:#   diagonal marker intentionally contacts two sides. The solver now infers a diagonal from the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2936:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:51:#   for diagonal rays. The new extension translates the entire marker bbox by (±1, ±1) each\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2937:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:65:#   so acceptance means all chosen diagonal markers are simultaneously legal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2938:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:68:# - A human can see several corner-attached seeds around the same '+', plus one long diagonal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2939:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:69:#   exemplar somewhere in the grid. That makes the diagonal repetition rule and the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2940:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:74:# - Generator forbids 4-neighbor contacts between foreign structures, so the diagonal strips do\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2941:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:83:#   preserving only the diagonal strips.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2942:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:87:#   horizontal side, which together encode one diagonal quadrant.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2943:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:156:def extend_diagonal_repeating_tile(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2944:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:166:    \"\"\"Translate a tile diagonally by one cell per step until the bbox no longer intersects.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2945:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:198:def _infer_diagonal_direction(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2946:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:204:    \"\"\"Infer one diagonal from the pair of orthogonal plus->marker contacts.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2947:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:230:    Extend every corner marker from each '+' as a diagonal periodic strip, then erase the source.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2948:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:236:      marker somewhere in the grid may already appear as a long diagonal strip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2949:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:240:      infer the corresponding diagonal quadrant.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2950:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:242:      step along the inferred diagonal until the grid boundary.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2951:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:246:    strip is just repeated one-cell diagonal shifts of that seed component, and the '+' itself is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2952:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:283:            direction = _infer_diagonal_direction(pts, plus_mask, H, W)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2953:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:289:            extend_diagonal_repeating_tile(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2954:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:358:def _project_diagonal_component(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2955:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:365:    \"\"\"Compute full diagonal strip cells, seed origin, and number of shifted copies.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2956:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:464:    \"\"\"Try to place one plus sprite with 2-4 diagonal marker rays.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2957:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:500:                    projected = _project_diagonal_component(H, W, plus_bbox, direction, tile)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2958:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:601:    - the scene should use at least 3 diagonal directions overall.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2959:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:369:    \"\"\"Return a thick anti-diagonal path band with a top-left template pocket.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2960:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2d0172a1/10/code.py:567:    \"\"\"Arrange children with tight non-diagonal layouts when a frame child is present.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2961:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2d0172a1/10/code.py:586:        mode = random.choice((\"vertical\", \"horizontal\", \"diagonal\"))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2962:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/45/code.py:64:#     - diagonal motion still needs anti-corner-cut checks for the whole 2x2 anchor, not just one cell\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2963:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/4/code.py:8:#    alongside phase, then leave diagonally. Here that middle phase is removed entirely. In local coordinates\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2964:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/4/code.py:15:#    diagonal phases to be non-empty preserves a visibly sharp V. Restricting `p1` to a small set {1,2} keeps\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2965:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/4/code.py:216:    - Repaint the segment as exactly two diagonal-forward monotone phases: approach that apex, then immediately\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2966:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/4/code.py:217:      flip to the opposite diagonal and exit. There is no straight-middle phase and no edge-following run.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2967:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/4/code.py:335:        assert 0 < split < len(step_classes), \"both diagonal phases must be non-empty\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2968:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/21/code.py:301:    - Elsewhere: one 2x2 end block and one thick path-color band crossing the board diagonally.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2969:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2d0172a1/21/code.py:23:#      then displayed as a down-right diagonal chain.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2970:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2d0172a1/21/code.py:32:#      becomes the first diagonal child; the enclosing rectangle is then expanded to the smallest scaled\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2971:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2d0172a1/21/code.py:33:#      copy of the input frame ratio that can still hold the diagonal child layout with a 1-cell moat.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2972:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2d0172a1/21/code.py:48:#      Invalid now: sibling order depends only on radial distance, so layout becomes a diagonal rank display.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2973:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2d0172a1/21/code.py:53:#      diagonal items.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2974:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2d0172a1/21/code.py:277:    - Inside each frame, sort direct children by increasing centroid distance to the frame center and place them as a down-right diagonal chain with one background cell between consecutive canonical objects.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2975:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2d0172a1/21/code.py:627:        mode = random.choice((\"vertical\", \"horizontal\", \"diagonal\", \"scatter\"))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2976:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2d0172a1/21/code.py:635:        elif mode == \"diagonal\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2977:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/5/code.py:19:#    as a sequence of obstacle-modules: approach diagonally on the current side,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2978:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/5/code.py:20:#    skim forward along the obstacle's outer side, then cross diagonally past the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2979:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/5/code.py:22:#    between multiple blockers before its final diagonal tail.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2980:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/5/code.py:329:      second-nearest (and possibly third), then keep the final diagonal heading until length runs out.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2981:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:18:#    - D1: the path is now diagonal, so each copy is shifted by (±1, ±1).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2982:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:19:#    - D6: the ray no longer ends at the frame; it stops when the next diagonal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2983:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:23:#    notch cell, so the occupied notch identifies one of four diagonals:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2984:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:33:#    the clue ray into sparse diagonal dots, while a 2x2 seed would self-overlap\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2985:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:34:#    under unit diagonal shifts and create color-consistency ambiguity. Dominos\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2986:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:35:#    keep the diagonal repetition visually obvious and still allow both 1-color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2987:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:42:#      boundary-complete ray needed no further growth. Here a full diagonal clue\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2988:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:50:#    a diagonal domino ray and a blocker domino. Exact overlap is forbidden, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2989:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:54:#    In each sample, one ray is already expanded as a long diagonal staircase and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2990:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:57:#    both \"use the corner to choose a diagonal\" and \"stop at the blocker\" visible\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2991:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:140:    \"\"\"Return per-diagonal notch data for one plus component.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2992:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:172:    Recover the diagonal direction and the local 2-cell seed domino.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2993:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:254:def extend_repeating_tile_diagonally_until_blocked(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2994:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:263:    \"\"\"Repeat a 2-cell seed by unit diagonal translations until the next copy is blocked.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2995:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:293:    Extend corner-anchored marker dominos along diagonal rays, stopping at blockers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2996:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:301:      the corresponding diagonals.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2997:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:305:      one of the four diagonal directions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2998:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:307:      orthogonal neighbor, then copy the seed by repeated unit diagonal shifts.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2999:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:311:    Key insight: The seed's occupied corner notch determines the diagonal, while\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3000:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:346:            extend_repeating_tile_diagonally_until_blocked(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3001:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:358:# --------------- generator (output-first, diagonal + collision-stop) ---------------\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3002:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:394:    raise ValueError(\"direction must be diagonal\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3003:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:431:    \"\"\"Cells for the first `units` diagonal copies, including the seed at k=0.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3004:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:476:    \"\"\"Maximum number of full diagonal copies that fit before touching the frame.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3005:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:508:    \"\"\"Place one plus, one diagonal ray, and one blocker, or return None.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3006:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:15:      - directions are diagonal only, so every legend is the 6x7 diagonal template\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3007:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:18:      - rooms are generated as plain rectangles so the diagonal rebound pattern is visually clean:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3008:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:40:          zigzag endpoint produced by one or more diagonal bounces\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3009:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:45:      - directions: exactly 4 diagonals\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3010:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:57:      Generator preserves that exactly with the original 6x7 diagonal legend template.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3011:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:66:    - diagonal movement assumes corner-cut prevention via both orthogonal support cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3012:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:79:    - the diagonal-only restriction is visible immediately because all legends share the 6x7\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3013:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:80:      diagonal shape and no cardinal legend appears\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3014:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:95:    - because samples all show diagonal legends plus reflected endpoints, a human can infer that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3015:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:99:    - solver expects legends to decode to diagonal vectors in generated data\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3016:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:416:    Move yellow pixels inside sealed rooms according to corner legends, but only along diagonal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3017:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:424:    - Each legend contains center and indicator marks whose offset encodes one of the four diagonal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3018:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:429:      legend to get the initial diagonal direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3019:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:432:    - Simulate up to a fixed number of diagonal steps. When the next step hits a wall, flip the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3020:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:438:      \"the far wall.\" You must track a finite diagonal reflection path inside the room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3021:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:25:#      each usable object is a hollow diagonal funnel whose single spike is a bbox corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3022:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:28:#      Example: suppose a NW-pointing cup has 4 interior payload pixels and the diagonal cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3023:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:31:#      D1 alone would instead paint diagonal step1..step4 continuously.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3024:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:32:#      This combo erases the interior payload, walks diagonally one step at a time, paints only\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3025:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:37:#      \"advance diagonally\" decides which cell is inspected,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3026:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:41:#    - Only four diagonal directions are used; that keeps the rule legible while still requiring\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3027:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:44:#      so the sample set cannot silently degrade into plain diagonal emission or plain dashed rays.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3028:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:51:#    - Original mouth flooding used one opposite side only. For diagonal funnels that is insufficient;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3029:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:55:#      1. use a diagonal step vector,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3030:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:62:#    - The entire diagonal corridor to the edge is reserved in `occ_path`, including skipped cells,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3031:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:68:#    - From a few examples, the solver sees a corner-spike diagonal funnel, then in the output a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3032:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:78:#      and lies exactly on the continuation of the launched diagonal ray.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3033:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:82:#    - Assumption: the first non-bg cell on the launch diagonal is the stopping obstacle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3034:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:207:    Eject content pixels from diagonal cup-frames outward along a 45-degree tail direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3035:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:210:    - Detect the spike corner of each diagonal funnel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3036:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:213:    - Traverse diagonally outward cell by cell:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3037:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:296:    Build a diagonal funnel whose spike is the NW corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3038:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:377:    \"\"\"Find a placement whose diagonal corridor visibly demonstrates dash+collision.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3039:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/28/code.py:10:#    - One U endpoint has an outward-diagonal first step; that visible local direction is the D8/3 signal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3040:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/28/code.py:19:#    - The matched side is readable from shape alone: one endpoint immediately steps outward-diagonally while\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3041:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/28/code.py:323:    - Inspect the first step from each endpoint: the endpoint whose first move goes outward-diagonally marks\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3042:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2d0172a1/19/code.py:591:    mode = random.choice((\"vertical\", \"horizontal\", \"diagonal\"))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3043:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/4/code.py:312:    \"\"\"Return a thick anti-diagonal path band that touches all four borders.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3044:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:31:#      drilling; diagonal disambiguation is unnecessary noise here.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3045:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/16/code.py:15:#    the arms of a '+'. In this combo, the seed instead sits in one diagonal corner\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3046:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/16/code.py:17:#    keep diagonal repetition clean, seeds are only 1x2 or 2x1. Each next unit is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3047:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/16/code.py:18:#    shifted by exactly (dr,dc) = (±1,±1), producing a zipper-like diagonal chain.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3048:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/16/code.py:21:#    Finally, a dedicated obstacle color occupies the footprint of the next diagonal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3049:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/16/code.py:26:#    Restricting seeds to 2 cells prevents diagonal self-overlap, keeps the mirror\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3050:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/16/code.py:32:#      That breaks here; seeds touch pluses only diagonally, so component lookup must\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3051:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/16/code.py:35:#      now recovered from which diagonal corner window contains the 2-cell seed.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3052:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/16/code.py:37:#      diagonal steps are by unit, not by rows/cols alone, and odd/even units use\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3053:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/16/code.py:42:#    - A pre-expanded clue component is now a long diagonal chain, not a compact seed.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3054:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/16/code.py:46:#    The generator is output-first. For each plus it chooses a diagonal direction, a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3055:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/16/code.py:49:#    obstacle overlaps existing objects, or if a future plus would become diagonally\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3056:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/16/code.py:53:#    visible: the clue leaves from a d